{"name":"Stardust Ballroom","hex":"#dacfd4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stardust","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Small fragments of dustlike material found in space; specifically, a type of cosmic dust that formed from cooling gases ejected from presolar stars, which was then incorporated into the cloud from which the Solar System condensed.","Small fragments of dustlike material found in space; specifically, a type of cosmic dust that formed from cooling gases ejected from presolar stars, which was then incorporated into the cloud from which the Solar System condensed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stardust"},{"term":"ballroom","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large room used for dancing and banquets.","A type of elegant dance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in ballroom dancing."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ballroom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ballroom","blocks":[{"text":"A ballroom or ballhall is a large room for holding large formal parties called balls. Traditionally, most balls were held in private residences; many mansions and palaces, especially historic mansions and palaces, contain one or more ballrooms. In other large houses, a large room such as the main drawing room, long gallery, or hall may double as a ballroom, but a good ballroom should have the right type of flooring, such as hardwood flooring or stone flooring .. For most styles of modern dance, a wooden sprung floor offers the best surface."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Catherine_Palace_ballroom.jpg/330px-Catherine_Palace_ballroom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ballroom","wikidata":"Q805353"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Oranjezaal_na_de_restauratie-_overzicht_noordoosthoek%2C_met_de_hele_oostwand_-_%27s-Gravenhage_-_204